Don't compile pnpm-cli's source checkout path into the wasm build.

Reason: current_source_pnpm_version() walks up from env!("CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR")
to find the checkout's pnpm11/pnpm/package.json, for pnpm run from its own
source tree. env! is a string literal, so --remap-path-prefix doesn't reach
it: pnpm.wasm carried <srcdir>/pnpm-<commit>/pnpm/crates/cli, and its bytes
depended on the directory it was built in (homescoop#522). pnpm.wasm never
runs from a checkout; at runtime the lookup only tried paths like
/home/runner/…/pnpm11/pnpm/package.json and their parents. On wasm the
function answers None, which is what it found there anyway.

Upstream: not filed (Lars decides).
removeWhen: upstream stops embedding CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR in non-test code.

--- a/pnpm/crates/cli/src/cli_args/package_manager.rs
+++ b/pnpm/crates/cli/src/cli_args/package_manager.rs
@@ -197,8 +197,15 @@
 }
 
 pub(crate) fn current_source_pnpm_version() -> Option<String> {
-    let manifest_dir = Path::new(env!("CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR"));
-    manifest_dir.ancestors().find_map(pnpm_version_from)
+    // pnpm.wasm never runs from its source checkout, and env! would compile
+    // the checkout's absolute path into it.
+    #[cfg(target_family = "wasm")]
+    return None;
+    #[cfg(not(target_family = "wasm"))]
+    {
+        let manifest_dir = Path::new(env!("CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR"));
+        manifest_dir.ancestors().find_map(pnpm_version_from)
+    }
 }
 
